From e8049a78b10d6468551a75676f2c4c7032b5decb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:23:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [EME] Add an external W3C CDM backend for the GStreamer port

WPE builds the GStreamer EME framework but, with Thunder off, registers
no CDMFactory or CDMProxyFactory for GStreamer and ships no decryptor
element, so Encrypted Media Extensions do not work. The cross-platform
ClearKey CDM is compiled yet never registered on this port.

Add ENABLE_EXTERNAL_CDM, a backend that registers as a peer of Thunder
and, for this first step, offers the org.w3.clearkey key system only. It
decrypts in process with libgcrypt, resolving keys by key id from the
shared CDMProxy key store that the ClearKey session fills. The feature
defaults off and depends on ENCRYPTED_MEDIA.

The EME-level ClearKey key handling, CENC key-id extraction and JSON Web
Key parsing, is reused from the existing ClearKey CDM by promoting four
helpers to the WebCore::ClearKey namespace, so only the GStreamer proxy,
the decryptor element and the backend shells are new. The key handle
value stays the raw key bytes, so KeyHandleValueVariant is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>

---

